/* --- Cheat how-to + browser hints --- */
"guide.cheats.title" = "How cheat codes work";
"guide.cheats.intro" = "A code is active as soon as you add it. If nothing happens in the game, it is almost always the first step below that is missing.";
"guide.cheats.step1" = "Tap Browse cheat codes and pick one. The code and its name fill in for you, then tap Add code.";
"guide.cheats.step2" = "Most Game Boy Advance and DS games need a Master Code, sometimes called Enable Code, added and switched on FIRST. Without it the other codes do nothing at all. They are marked with a key and shown at the top of the list.";
"guide.cheats.step3" = "The green circle next to a code switches it on and off. Grey means off.";
"guide.cheats.step4" = "Some codes only take effect after leaving and re-entering an area, or after the next screen change.";
"guide.cheats.step5" = "Codes are written for one version of a game. A code from a different region or revision may do nothing, or behave strangely.";
"guide.cheats.footer" = "Your progress is saved before the first code is added, so you can always go back with Restore pre-cheat save.";
"cheats.browse.masterHint" = "Codes marked with a key must be switched on before the others work.";
"cheats.browse.notFound" = "This game was not recognised from its file name. Search for it below.";

"guide.cheats.step6" = "Many codes need a button press to fire, and the code's own name says which: for example Press SELECT to Restore Time. That name is kept when you add the code, so read it in your list.";

"settings.cheatDB.upToDate" = "All your games are available offline";
"settings.cheatDB.noGames" = "Add a game to your library first.";

